cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or data, please cite them as below."
title: "Erdős Problem #160 small values, and unlabeled graphs counted by treewidth"
authors:
  - family-names: Schluer
    given-names: Scott
abstract: >-
  First exact small values for Erdős Problem #160: M(3..6) = 12, 22, 35, 53 (so h(N) is exact for N <= 76),
  with M(7) >= 76 and M(8) >= 97, certified by checked DRAT/LRAT proofs. OEIS A362908 (graphs with treewidth 2)
  extended to n = 100 by an exact generating function verified against exhaustive enumeration for n <= 14; new terms of
  A362907 and rows 10-11 of A263294; counts of connected and all K4-minor-free graphs. Produced by a team of AI agents
  (Anthropic's Claude) with independent verification, operated by Scott Schluer.
date-released: 2026-10-19
